1
00:00:00,244 --> 00:00:01,907
Same AI, same exam…

2
00:00:02,001 --> 00:00:03,805
and a score 24 points higher.

3
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:06,425
It happened on WebArena, a test where

4
00:00:06,367 --> 00:00:08,489
AI navigates real websites.

5
00:00:08,690 --> 00:00:09,432
Same model:

6
00:00:09,586 --> 00:00:11,802
from 48 up to 72%.

7
00:00:12,216 --> 00:00:13,477
They didn't change its brain.

8
00:00:13,678 --> 00:00:14,916
They changed its harness.

9
00:00:15,328 --> 00:00:17,391
The harness is everything around the model:

10
00:00:17,545 --> 00:00:20,740
tools, memory, instructions, and a loop to

11
00:00:20,552 --> 00:00:22,038
review and retry.

12
00:00:22,472 --> 00:00:23,556
Think of it like this:

13
00:00:23,627 --> 00:00:24,983
the model is the engine.

14
00:00:25,184 --> 00:00:27,742
But without wheels, steering or brakes, it

15
00:00:27,554 --> 00:00:29,051
won't win any race.

16
00:00:29,241 --> 00:00:30,502
The harness is the car.

17
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:32,150
And it's not a one-off:

18
00:00:32,339 --> 00:00:34,579
on another coding test, the same model

19
00:00:34,391 --> 00:00:37,126
scores 80% with its vendor's harness, and

20
00:00:36,938 --> 00:00:38,860
59% with a neutral one.

21
00:00:39,268 --> 00:00:41,013
So when you see an AI leaderboard,

22
00:00:41,096 --> 00:00:42,959
don't just ask which model it is.

23
00:00:43,148 --> 00:00:43,631
Ask:

24
00:00:43,466 --> 00:00:44,303
which harness?

25
00:00:44,708 --> 00:00:47,326
Because today, the bottleneck isn't the model.

26
00:00:47,515 --> 00:00:48,375
It's the harness.

27
00:00:48,792 --> 00:00:50,643
Save it, and share it with whoever

28
00:00:50,455 --> 00:00:52,105
picks the AI at your company.

